# Planner twin ratchet (R1188-U16).
#
# The ceiling on functions that a module under js/agentic/ exports with no Rust
# twin: no `fn` in rust/src/ spelled as the snake_case form of the name, and no
# `fn`, `const`, `static`, `struct` or `enum` its doc comment cites in a
# `Mirrors` line, unless its doc comment says it stands for a Rust built-in or
# for an item of a crate the Rust root depends on: "Rust built-in" or "Rust
# dependency", then the feature in backticks, such as str::char_indices or
# serde_json::from_str. Every exported planner function has a twin since R1188-U16
# reached 0, so a new one cannot land in JavaScript alone.
# scripts/check-planner-twins.mjs fails above the ceiling and asks for the
# ceiling to be lowered below it, so the number only falls.
#
# `exempt` lists a module that exists only on the JavaScript side by design,
# with the reason. A module that ports a Rust module is never exempt.
planner_twin_ratchet
  no_twin_ceiling 0
  exempt js/agentic/host.mjs
    reason "The host port the planner reads files, the clock and the network through; native Rust calls std directly."
  exempt js/agentic/node-host.mjs
    reason "The Node.js adapter behind the host port (node:fs, fetch); native Rust needs no adapter."
  exempt js/agentic/write_str.mjs
    reason "Rust str and char semantics for JavaScript strings (UTF-8 offsets, Unicode trimming); Rust has them built in."
  exempt js/agentic/crate/rust_str.mjs
    reason "Rust str and char semantics for JavaScript strings (split_whitespace, is_alphanumeric); Rust has them built in."
